---
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProjectHeader from '../../components/ProjectHeader.astro';
import ProjectNav from '../../components/ProjectNav.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Stepper from '../../components/Stepper.astro';
const entry = (await getEntry('research', 'scaling-up'))!;
---
<Base title={entry.data.title} description={entry.data.summary}>
  <ProjectHeader entry={entry} />

  <Section num="1" title="The idea" lede="Stop describing what a binary looks like. Learn what normal looks like, and keep whatever is not.">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The velocity-offset search in step 03 only finds what it is told to look for: a shifted or double-peaked broad line. A variational autoencoder learns a compressed representation of every DESI spectrum and how to rebuild it. Spectra that follow the common patterns are rebuilt well; artefacts and rare physics, including binary signatures, are rebuilt badly or land in empty parts of the latent space. Nicolaou et al. (2026) showed this on about 200,000 DESI spectra of galaxies, quasars and stars.</p>
        <p>For binaries the payoff is a selection that does not depend on hand-picked thresholds, applied uniformly to DESI DR3, with the anomalies cross-matched against the step 03 candidates.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="side">
        <div><div class="mono"><b>Builds on</b></div>Liang et al. 2023; Nicolaou et al. 2026 and earlier anomaly-detection work on survey spectra.</div>
        <div><div class="mono"><b>Status</b></div>Starts after the DR1 candidate catalogue is out.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section num="2" title="How it works">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1200 260" class="vae" role="img" aria-label="Diagram of a variational autoencoder scoring spectra">
      <g font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="12" fill="#6b645c">
        <rect x="30" y="70" width="200" height="120" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#e3ddd4" />
        <polyline points="45,160 70,150 90,155 110,90 125,150 150,140 170,145 185,100 200,145 215,150" fill="none" stroke="#1a1714" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="130" y="215" text-anchor="middle">input spectrum</text>
        <path d="M250 70 L400 110 L400 150 L250 190 Z" fill="#fff8f7" stroke="#8b1e2a" />
        <text x="325" y="135" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b1e2a">encoder</text>
        <rect x="430" y="105" width="120" height="50" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1a1714" />
        <text x="490" y="135" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1a1714">latent z</text>
        <text x="490" y="215" text-anchor="middle">a few numbers per spectrum</text>
        <path d="M580 110 L730 70 L730 190 L580 150 Z" fill="#fff8f7" stroke="#8b1e2a" />
        <text x="655" y="135" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b1e2a">decoder</text>
        <rect x="760" y="70" width="200" height="120" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#e3ddd4" />
        <polyline points="775,160 800,150 820,155 840,95 855,150 880,140 900,145 915,105 930,145 945,150" fill="none" stroke="#1a1714" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <polyline points="775,160 800,150 820,155 840,90 855,150 880,140 900,145 915,100 930,145 945,150" fill="none" stroke="#8b1e2a" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
        <text x="860" y="215" text-anchor="middle">reconstruction</text>
        <rect x="1000" y="95" width="170" height="70" fill="#1a1714" />
        <text x="1085" y="124" text-anchor="middle" fill="#faf8f4">anomaly score</text>
        <text x="1085" y="145" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c9c2b8">reconstruction error</text>
        <line x1="960" y1="130" x2="998" y2="130" stroke="#1a1714" />
        <line x1="230" y1="130" x2="248" y2="130" stroke="#1a1714" />
        <line x1="550" y1="130" x2="578" y2="130" stroke="#1a1714" />
        <line x1="400" y1="130" x2="428" y2="130" stroke="#1a1714" />
        <line x1="730" y1="130" x2="758" y2="130" stroke="#1a1714" />
      </g>
    </svg>
    <div class="gap"></div>
    <Stepper label="Plan" steps={[
      { title: 'Train on DR3', detail: 'Fit the autoencoder on the broad-line galaxy and quasar spectra of DESI DR3, with the redshift removed so that the same line lands in the same place for every object.' },
      { title: 'Score every spectrum', detail: 'Reconstruction error and position in latent space give each object an anomaly score. Artefacts are identified and set aside; the physical anomalies remain.' },
      { title: 'Cross-match with step 03', detail: 'The velocity-offset candidates are a labelled set: they show where binaries sit in latent space and let the search look for neighbours that thresholds missed.' },
      { title: 'Follow up', detail: 'Repeat spectroscopy and light curves for the strongest anomalies, the same time-domain checks used in step 03.' },
      { title: 'Forecast', detail: 'A candidate population with a known selection function goes into LISA and pulsar-timing event-rate estimates alongside the dual AGN census.' },
    ]} />
  </Section>

  <Section num="3" title="Where it leads">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Steps 01 to 03 each cover one separation scale. This one closes the loop: a uniform, survey-wide selection of binary candidates that, together with the kiloparsec census and the ASTRID forecasts, gives the electromagnetic side of the massive black hole merger rate from the first pairing to the final gravitational-wave signal.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="side">
        <div><div class="mono"><b>Before</b></div><a href="/research/mbhb-desi/">Step 03 · The close pairs</a></div>
        <div><div class="mono"><b>Overview</b></div><a href="/research/">The thesis</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <ProjectNav current="scaling-up" />
</Base>
<style>
  .gap { height: 28px; }
  .vae { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
</style>
